  "scope": "Actual rooted isomorphism classes of countable connected locally finite SimpleGraphs; actual walk-ball cylinders and their generated sigma algebra. Uniform rooting of the actual disjoint unions of m+1 copies of P3, taking the induced reachable component, has exactly the P3 uniform-root law for every m; vertex counts tend to infinity and local weak convergence holds. A genuine radius-two cylinder union has limiting mass one and mass zero under every measure concentrated on vertex-transitive graphs. No arbitrary measure-valued mixture of such measures can have this law as barycentre; therefore the asserted extreme-point decomposition with transitive support is false. No extremality assertion or finite linear-program surrogate is used."
